DPIGate
=======

DPIGate was published as GoodByeDPI-Plus before version 3.0.0.

This project is a derivative work of GoodbyeDPI by ValdikSS
(https://github.com/ValdikSS/GoodbyeDPI), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

The following files were modified from the original GoodbyeDPI source:
  - windows/goodbyedpi.c      — added --only-programs / --debug-proc flags
                                and per-program gate logic
  - windows/Makefile          — added -liphlpapi for GetExtendedTcpTable

The following files were added:
  - windows/proctrack.c       — per-program 5-tuple→PID→exe→whitelist tracker
                                with WinDivert FLOW layer integration, hot-reload
                                watcher thread, and connection seeding
  - windows/proctrack.h       — public API for the per-program tracker
  - windows/programs.txt      — default whitelist (editable)
  - windows/start.ps1         — PowerShell launcher with DNS redirect config
  - windows/install.ps1       — Start Menu shortcut installer with tray launch
  - windows/uninstall.ps1     — removes shortcut, scheduled tasks, and processes
  - windows/setup.iss         — Inno Setup installer script
  - .github/                  — GitHub Actions CI workflow and issue templates
  - README.md                 — project documentation


The Linux port lives in the linux/ directory. The engine files below are
ports of the original GoodbyeDPI sources (same algorithms, WinDivert calls
replaced with NFQUEUE/raw-socket equivalents):

  - linux/goodbyedpi.c     — port of windows/goodbyedpi.c
  - linux/checksum.c       — replaces WinDivert's checksum helper; has no
                             windows/ counterpart (on Windows the checksum
                             work is done by WinDivertHelperCalcChecksums)
  - linux/blackwhitelist.c — port of windows/blackwhitelist.c
  - linux/ttltrack.c       — port of windows/ttltrack.c
  - linux/fakepackets.c    — port of windows/fakepackets.c
  - linux/dnsredir.c       — port of windows/dnsredir.c

Added for the Linux port:

  - linux/packet_io_linux.c/.h — NFQUEUE capture/modify/reinject
  - linux/proctrack_linux.c/.h  — per-program 5-tuple→PID tracker (sock_diag)
  - linux/rawsend_linux.c/.h    — raw-socket fake packet sender
  - linux/utils/getline.c/.h, repl_str.c/.h, uthash.h — bundled utility sources
  - linux/start.sh, kill.sh, reaper.sh, tray-launcher.sh, tray.py,
    dns_detect.py, installer-gui.py, install.sh, uninstall.sh, vm-diag.sh,
    lib/platform.sh, lib/wizard-zenity.sh, scripts/ — launchers, the
    graphical setup wizard, installer/uninstaller, diagnostics and the
    cross-distro portability layer
  - docs/linux-port-notes.md, docs/vm-diagnostics.md — Linux design and
    diagnostics notes

The startup-script concept was inspired by keift/goodbyedpi
(https://github.com/keift/goodbyedpi).

WinDivert (https://github.com/basil00/Divert) by basil00 is bundled
as pre-built binaries (WinDivert.dll, WinDivert*.sys) under the
windows/x86/ and windows/x86_64/ directories and is used under its
LGPL/MIT license.

